{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794445496,"nonce":"xolD2vRHaoJrS7nbzPCAc4haK58=","title":"Rotated glyphs are drawn smeared","message":"A card with the label \"Card\" turned 35 degrees by `.rotate_deg(35.0)` (CSS transform, no binding involved) draws the glyphs broken: fragments above the \"C\", a smeared \"d\" ascender, stray marks beside the \"a\". A bound rotation draws the same pixels now that it reaches the text (40fc670), so this is the glyph path under a rotation affine and not the binding.\n\nNot diagnosed. The glyph quads are placed through `css_affine` in the text pipeline; the fragments look like the rotated glyph sampled inside an axis-aligned quad that is too small for it. Reproduce: a `card(true).rotate_deg(35.0)` in the headless harness and read the frame, or the contact sheet BLINC_ANIM_PATHS_OUT writes for the label test.\n\nText under a small rotation (a few degrees) looks fine; it gets worse as the angle grows.","files":null}]}